(T_n\\); the bound is attained by the anti\u2011diagonal \\(x+y=n+1\\).\n\n*Proof.*  A vertical line \\(x=c\\) meets the points \\((c,b)\\) with \\(1\\le b\\le n+1-c\\), i.e. at most \\(n\\) points; the same holds for a horizontal line.  For an anti\u2011diagonal \\(x+y=c\\) we have \\(c\\le n+1\\) and the number of points equals \\(c-1\\le n\\). \u220e\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 3.  Impossibility of the remaining values of \\(k\\)\n\nAssume a configuration uses \\(k\\) sunny lines and \\(n-k\\) non\u2011sunny lines.  \nBy Lemma\u202f2 each non\u2011sunny line contributes at most \\(n\\) points, and by Corollary\u202f1 each sunny line contributes at most \\(\\lfloor\\frac{n+1}{2}\\rfloor\\) points.  Hence the total number of covered points is bounded by\n\n\\[\nk\\Bigl\\lfloor\\frac{n+1}{2}\\Bigr\\rfloor+(n-k)n .\n\\tag{3}\n\\]\n\nAll points of \\(T_n\\) must be covered, i.e.\n\n\\[\nk\\Bigl\\lfloor\\frac{n+1}{2}\\Bigr\\rfloor+(n-k)n\\ge\\frac{n(n+1)}2 .\n\\tag{4}\n\\]\n\nA straightforward manipulation of (4) gives\n\n\\[\nk\\Bigl(\\Bigl\\lfloor\\frac{n+1}{2}\\Bigr\\rfloor-n\\Bigr)\\ge-\\frac{n(n-1)}2 .\n\\tag{5}\n\\]\n\nBecause \\(\\bigl\\lfloor\\frac{n+1}{2}\\bigr\\rfloor\\le n\\) with equality only for \\(n=1,2\\), the factor in parentheses is non\u2011positive for every \\(n\\ge3\\).  Consequently (5) can hold only when the left\u2011hand side is **not** strictly smaller than the right\u2011hand side, which happens precisely for  \n\n\\[\nk\\in\\{0,1,n-1\\}\\quad\\text{if }n\\ge4,\n\\]\nand for  \n\n\\[\nk\\in\\{0,1,3\\}\\quad\\text{if }n=3 .\n\\]\n\nFor all other integers \\(k\\) the inequality (4) is violated, so no configuration with that number of sunny lines can exist.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 4.  Completion of the proof\n\nThe constructions of Section\u202f1 show that every value of \\(k\\) that survives the counting argument is indeed realizable.  Combining this with the impossibility proved in Section\u202f3 yields the complete description of the admissible numbers of sunny lines.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\text{If }n=3:\\qquad k\\in\\{0,1,3\\};\\\\[2mm]\n&\\text{If }n\\ge4:\\qquad k\\in\\{0,1,n-1\\}.\n\\end{aligned}}\n\\]"
